{"parentUuid":"e4cffcf4-87c1-4f6b-a276-d7ef316f3d2d","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a37cf00dce550f097","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01YC6ibZiE4957rw8TDYu4bR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AEuAKVR1Tu7hctNtGAEc7N","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"CP-SAT diff_n no_overlap_2d propagator bounds consistency placement"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8139,"cache_read_input_tokens":13113,"output_tokens":344,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8139},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":344,"cache_read_input_tokens":13113,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8139,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8139,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caorc7YHCCR6aAgK6KWFN","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"a505258e-1199-4588-a498-e1eb08c6e1cb","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:41:00.081Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"e2cad591-073c-4917-a312-5b6973b319e8","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"fa4d4bc6-e2b2-445f-8cd0-cc97f0106215","agentId":"a37cf00dce550f097","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AGgfWrfAjpGWU6HaUjVYpn","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"2D rectangle packing preprocessing dominance rules reduction OR-tools CP-SAT\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - ktnr/BinPacking2D: Exact solutions for two-dimensional bin packing problems by branch-and-cut · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ktnr/BinPacking2D\"},{\"title\":\"Advanced Modeling - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/04B_advanced_modelling.html\"},{\"title\":\"Yet Another Math Programming Consultant: 2d bin packing with Google OR-Tools CP-SAT, how to fix?\",\"url\":\"http://yetanothermathprogrammingconsultant.blogspot.com/2021/02/2d-bin-packing-with-google-or-tools-cp.html\"},{\"title\":\"Exact Solution Techniques for Two-dimensional Cutting and Packing\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/am/pii/S0377221720306111\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"Positions and covering: A two-stage methodology to obtain optimal solutions for the 2d-bin packing problem | PLOS One\",\"url\":\"https://journals.plos.org/plosone/article?id=10.1371%2Fjournal.pone.0229358\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) A SAT-based Method for Solving the Two-dimensional Strip Packing Problem\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/220445013_A_SAT-based_Method_for_Solving_the_Two-dimensional_Strip_Packing_Problem\"},{\"title\":\"Solving the parallel processor scheduling and bin packing problems\",\"url\":\"https://optimization-online.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/Solving-the-PPSP-and-the-BPP-with-contiguity-constraints-2.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"2D Bin Packing\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/gMgPBryj1wA\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT: Parameter documentation NoOverlap2D, Cumulative · google/or-tools · Discussion #3107\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/discussions/3107\"}]\n\nI've completed the web search for your query about 2D rectangle packing with preprocessing, dominance rules reduction, OR-Tools, and CP-SAT. Here's a summary of the relevant findings:\n\n## Key Results\n\n**Preprocessing and Dominance Rules:**\n\nPreprocessing routines for 2D bin packing include filtering of large items, determining incompatible items, fixing and restricting item assignment through a conflict graph based on item incompatibility, and different bin-specific placement point pattern strategies.\n\nBranch and bound algorithms for strip packing problems develop lower bounds based on integer formulations and geometric considerations, and reduce the tree search with dominance criteria.\n\n**OR-Tools CP-SAT Implementation:**\n\nThe 2D-OPP (orthogonal packing problem) subproblem is solved via CP, similar to established methods, with or-tools having most of the described propagations.\n\nCP-SAT's add_no_overlap_2d constraint is used to prevent overlaps between intervals on two dimensions, for example, for packing rectangles.\n\n**Dominant Positions:**\n\nThe main idea is to generate the dominant set of valid positions where items can be placed in the bin; from the infinite set of all positions an item can take, only a finite set is constructed that guarantees optimality of the solution.\n\nThe search results show that these techniques are actively used in solving 2D packing problems, with OR-Tools' CP-SAT solver being a practical implementation platform.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"9f09b18f-fc14-4509-ae82-e87433d41996","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:41:06.155Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e2cad591-073c-4917-a312-5b6973b319e8","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"e4cffcf4-87c1-4f6b-a276-d7ef316f3d2d","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"fa4d4bc6-e2b2-445f-8cd0-cc97f0106215","agentId":"a37cf00dce550f097","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01R6tPXVNRL6sfLuuZd4wjHS","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"bin packing dominance criteria preprocessing Martello Toth Carlier\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"arXiv:1110.2209v1 [cs.AI] 10 Oct 2011\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1110.2209\"},{\"title\":\"Solving the parallel processor scheduling and bin packing problems with contiguity constraints: Mathematical models and computational studies - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0377221724007161\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Lower bounds and reduction procedures for the bin packing problem\",\"url\":\"https://www.academia.edu/108860126/Lower_bounds_and_reduction_procedures_for_the_bin_packing_problem?uc-sb-sw=24937845\"},{\"title\":\"A HYBRID IMPROVEMENT HEURISTIC FOR THE ONE-DIMENSIONAL BIN PACKING PROBLEM\",\"url\":\"https://leeds-faculty.colorado.edu/glover/fred%20pubs/334%20-%20TS%20-%20bin%20packing%20-%20Ceslso.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Bin packing problems 23rd Belgian Mathematical Optimization Workshop\",\"url\":\"https://mathopt.be/Slides_LaRoche_Martello.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Exact and approximate size reduction for the bin packing problem with conflicts - Wassim Zahrouni, Hichem Kamoun, 2025\",\"url\":\"https://doi.org/10.1177/18724981241307388\"},{\"title\":\"Bin-Completion Algorithms for Multicontainer Packing and Covering Problems\",\"url\":\"https://www.ijcai.org/Proceedings/05/Papers/0891.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Bin Packing Problem - an overview | ScienceDirect Topics\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/computer-science/bin-packing-problem\"},{\"title\":\"A New Algorithm for Optimal Bin Packing Richard E. Korf\",\"url\":\"https://cdn.aaai.org/AAAI/2002/AAAI02-110.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Bin Completion Algorithms for Multicontainer Packing, ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.jair.org/index.php/jair/article/download/10492/25140/\"}]\n\nI've successfully performed the web search for \"bin packing dominance criteria preprocessing Martello Toth Carlier\". Here are the key findings:\n\n## Main Results:\n\n**Martello-Toth Dominance Criterion**: The Martello-Toth dominance criterion is a well-established approach used in bin-oriented search algorithms for bin packing. The Martello–Toth algorithm uses branch-and-bound methods which systematically explores feasible assignments and prunes the search space using dominance conditions.\n\n**Reduction Procedures and Preprocessing**: A Reduction Algorithm is a preprocessing procedure used to determine the optimal value of a subset of variables. Recent work generalizes Martello and Toth's dominance criterion, which was initially developed for the Bin Packing Problem.\n\n**Carlier's Contributions**: Carlier et al. claimed a dominance relation between their lower bounds and those of Boschetti and Mingozzi, though this dominance relation was later proven to be invalid.\n\n**Bin Completion and Dominance**: The bin completion strategy is based on feasible sets of objects that fit with respect to bin capacity, and the key property that makes bin completion more efficient is a dominance condition on the feasible completions of a bin.\n\nAdvanced preprocessing techniques and enhanced dominance criteria have been integrated to improve branch-and-bound algorithms for bin packing variants.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"3a00827d-c6bd-4386-b8f0-736dc8dac94b","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:41:06.973Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e4cffcf4-87c1-4f6b-a276-d7ef316f3d2d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"a505258e-1199-4588-a498-e1eb08c6e1cb","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"fa4d4bc6-e2b2-445f-8cd0-cc97f0106215","agentId":"a37cf00dce550f097","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AEuAKVR1Tu7hctNtGAEc7N","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP-SAT diff_n no_overlap_2d propagator bounds consistency placement\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Towards Bound Consistency for the No-Overlap Constraint Using MDDs\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2601.14784v1\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT: Parameter documentation NoOverlap2D, Cumulative · google/or-tools · Discussion #3107\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/discussions/3107\"},{\"title\":\"ortools.sat.python.cp_model API documentation\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/pdoc/ortools/sat/python/cp_model.html\"},{\"title\":\"Advanced Modeling - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/04B_advanced_modelling.html\"},{\"title\":\"Performance of packing problems · google/or-tools · Discussion #3177\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/discussions/3177\"},{\"title\":\"Placement of products on carrier, layer by layer with CP\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/d/topic/or-tools-discuss/T9DUhs2WCao\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://egon.cheme.cmu.edu/ewo/docs/CP-SAT%20and%20OR-Tools.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Yet Another Math Programming Consultant: 2d bin packing with Google OR-Tools CP-SAT, how to fix?\",\"url\":\"http://yetanothermathprogrammingconsultant.blogspot.com/2021/02/2d-bin-packing-with-google-or-tools-cp.html\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT for scheduling Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://schedulingseminar.com/presentations/SchedulingSeminar_LaurentPerron.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"View-based propagator derivation | Constraints | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10601-012-9133-z\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found related to your query about CP-SAT's `diff_n`, `no_overlap_2d` propagator, bounds consistency, and placement:\n\n## CP-SAT No-Overlap 2D Propagator\n\nThe `add_no_overlap_2d` constraint is used to prevent overlaps between intervals on two dimensions, for example, for packing rectangles. The `add_no_overlap_2d` constraint takes two lists of (optional) interval variables and ensures that for every i and j either x_intervals[i] and x_intervals[j] or y_intervals[i] and y_intervals[j] do not overlap.\n\n## Bounds Consistency and Propagation\n\nThe search results contain discussion of bound consistency (BC) approaches for no-overlap constraints. The number of nodes explored when using a bound-consistent propagator is measured, with closer to zero tree expansion meaning closer to bound consistent pruning.\n\n## Known Limitations\n\nThe no_overlap_2d propagator is acknowledged as poor, with developers noting they want to implement stronger versions but lack the time to do so. However, improvements have been made with new parameters like `use_energetic_reasoning_in_no_overlap_2d` and renaming of `use_cumulative_in_no_overlap_2d` to `use_timetabling_in_no_overlap_2d`.\n\nThe search results don't contain specific technical details about `diff_n` implementation or the exact consistency and placement mechanics you may be looking for. If you need more detailed technical documentation on these specific propagator components, you may want to consult the CP-SAT source code or more specialized constraint programming literature.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"ca129785-df1e-4312-acff-c1f35bfe0091","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:41:07.608Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a505258e-1199-4588-a498-e1eb08c6e1cb","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"c53bb6d9-ea12-4a29-921c-7e2b6bbb24c5","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"fa4d4bc6-e2b2-445f-8cd0-cc97f0106215","agentId":"a37cf00dce550f097","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AM6QorG9TjNyNUFELhmRLw","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"VLSI floorplanning placement preprocessing impossibility check survey 2024 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"A survey on VLSI Floorplanning: Its representation and modern approaches of optimization | IEEE Conference Publication | IEEE Xplore\",\"url\":\"https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/7192989\"},{\"title\":\"FloorSet - a VLSI Floorplanning Dataset with Design ...\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2405.05480\"},{\"title\":\"A survey on VLSI Floorplanning - Siliconvlsi\",\"url\":\"https://siliconvlsi.com/floorplanning/\"},{\"title\":\"A survey on VLSI Floorplanning: Its representation and modern approaches of optimization | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/308851945_A_survey_on_VLSI_Floorplanning_Its_representation_and_modern_approaches_of_optimization\"},{\"title\":\"[2405.05480] FloorSet -- a VLSI Floorplanning Dataset with Design Constraints of Real-World SoCs\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.05480\"},{\"title\":\"FLOORPLAN - VLSI TALKS\",\"url\":\"https://vlsitalks.com/physical-design/floorplan/\"},{\"title\":\"Challenges in Floorplanning and Macro Placement for Modern SoCs | Proceedings of the 2024 International Symposium on Physical Design\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3626184.3639695\"},{\"title\":\"FloorSet - a VLSI Floorplanning Dataset with Design Constraints of Real-World SoCs\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2405.05480v1\"},{\"title\":\"Physical Design: Methodologies and Developments\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2409.04726v1\"},{\"title\":\"VLSI Floorplanning Algorithm Based on Reinforcement Learning with Obstacles | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-50381-8_110\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, here are the findings related to VLSI floorplanning, placement, preprocessing, and impossibility checking for 2024-2025:\n\n## Recent VLSI Floorplanning Research (2024-2025)\n\n### Key Developments\n\nFloorplanning for systems-on-a-chip (SoCs) and its sub-systems is a crucial step of the physical design flow, representing a difficult combinatorial optimization problem. A typical large scale SoC with 120 partitions generates a search-space of nearly 10E250.\n\n### Recent Benchmarks and Datasets\n\nFloorSet presents two comprehensive datasets of synthetic fixed-outline floorplan layouts that reflect the distribution of real SoCs, with each dataset containing 1M training samples and 100 test samples, where FloorSet-Prime comprises fully-abutted rectilinear partitions and near-optimal wire-length.\n\n### Design Constraints and Feasibility\n\nThe key challenge of the floorplanning formulation lies in the requirement to satisfy hard design constraints, including the \"fixed-outline\" constraint for the SoC and its sub-systems, where a floorplan optimized for area without accounting for this constraint may fail to fit within the specified outline.\n\nAdditional constraints include boundary-constraints for partition alignment, grouping-constraints for physically abutted partitions, multi-instantiation constraints requiring shared shapes among instances, and pre-placement constraints specifying pre-defined locations of partitions.\n\n### Recent Works (2025)\n\nRecent publications from 2025 include HieRFP: A Hierarchical Recognition and Floorplanning Framework for Reusable Modules and IncreDFlip: Incremental Dataflow-Driven Macro Flipping for Efficient Macro Placement Refinement.\n\nHowever, the search results do not specifically address \"impossibility checks\" or detailed preprocessing methodologies for validating floorplan feasibility in recent surveys.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"0d7e8938-9d63-4f75-a1a9-ea8998133210","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:41:08.308Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c53bb6d9-ea12-4a29-921c-7e2b6bbb24c5","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
