{"parentUuid":"9704b4b0-99b6-4e2e-913c-257ed7c23815","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a37cf00dce550f097","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01PmqqSHrxADCbFVxinTpmcF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014kWC5hS48TsXqmajW4ZXkv","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"facility location grid placement multi-commodity flow precheck infeasibility"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2689,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3213,"cache_read_input_tokens":21252,"output_tokens":304,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3213},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2689,"output_tokens":304,"cache_read_input_tokens":21252,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3213,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3213,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaordAWuCE1NHwoYy5wRK","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"1ad534c7-df49-45f4-a8ba-889e1872eb51","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:41:13.453Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"0d6b8b6f-f3c5-49f4-8ce3-07371742c309","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"fa4d4bc6-e2b2-445f-8cd0-cc97f0106215","agentId":"a37cf00dce550f097","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013dAujmCeDAtVjZ9kHPUiEX","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"orthogonal packing problem feasibility test DFF dual feasible function lower bound\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"New data-dependent dual-feasible functions and lower bounds for a two-dimensional bin-packing problem | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/239396145_New_data-dependent_dual-feasible_functions_and_lower_bounds_for_a_two-dimensional_bin-packing_problem\"},{\"title\":\"New data-dependent dual-feasible functions and lower bounds for a two-dimensional bin-packing problem: International Journal of Production Research: Vol 47 , No 2 - Get Access\",\"url\":\"https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/00207540802426656\"},{\"title\":\"New reduction procedures and lower bounds for the two-dimensional bin packing problem with fixed orientation - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0305054805002765\"},{\"title\":\"Multidimensional dual-feasible functions and fast lower bounds for the vector packing problem - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0377221713006760\"},{\"title\":\"A General Framework for Bounds for Higher-Dimensional ...\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/cs/0402044\"},{\"title\":\"Discrete Optimization New lower bounds for bin packing problems with conﬂicts\",\"url\":\"https://www.math.u-bordeaux.fr/~fclautia/publications/EJOR-CDFF.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Using dual feasible functions to construct fast lower bounds for routing and location problems - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0166218X14002194\"},{\"title\":\"Using dual feasible functions to construct fast lower bounds for routing and location problems | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/273807731_Using_dual_feasible_functions_to_construct_fast_lower_bounds_for_routing_and_location_problems\"},{\"title\":\"New lower bounds for bin packing problems with conflicts\",\"url\":\"https://ideas.repec.org/a/eee/ejores/v206y2010i2p281-288.html\"},{\"title\":\"Exact method for the two-dimensional orthogonal packing problem\",\"url\":\"https://www.math.u-bordeaux.fr/~fclautia/publications/clautiaux_et_al_revised.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about the orthogonal packing problem, dual feasible functions (DFF), and lower bounds:\n\n## Overview\n\nConservative scales (CS) are a bounding technique for one- and higher-dimensional orthogonal packing problems, and they are modified item sizes such that the set of feasible packings is not reduced.\n\n## Dual Feasible Functions (DFF)\n\nDual-feasible functions (DFF) proposed by Johnson and data-dependent DFF (DDFF) can be used to obtain good lower bounds for bin-packing problems. A particular way of getting conservative scales is to construct them from (one-dimensional) dual feasible functions.\n\n## Feasibility Testing and Lower Bounds\n\nThe main problems include finding a packing with minimum height, packing items into the minimum number of bins, finding a packing of maximum value, and determining the existence of a feasible packing. Dual-feasible functions (DFF) can be used for computing lower bounds and can be applied to both dimensions of a bin packing instance.\n\n## Data-Dependent Functions\n\nData-dependent dual feasible functions (DDFF) are designed for a specific type of instances. The new concept of data-dependent dual feasible functions (DDFF) can be applied to a 2D bin packing instance.\n\nDue to their computational efficiency, dual-feasible functions are often implemented in branch-and-bound algorithms.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"4e954fbd-f64b-4f16-9924-6fa363cc0eeb","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:41:18.098Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0d6b8b6f-f3c5-49f4-8ce3-07371742c309","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"c44e796b-d5cd-4625-bfcf-1965dee1b368","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"fa4d4bc6-e2b2-445f-8cd0-cc97f0106215","agentId":"a37cf00dce550f097","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MwyZhQ43BQNV7uaGx2uGv9","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP-SAT presolve parameters cp_model_probing_level symmetry_level placement\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/cp_model_presolve.h at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/cp_model_presolve.h\"},{\"title\":\"cpmpy.solvers.ortools — CPMpy 0.9.24 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/latest/_modules/cpmpy/solvers/ortools.html\"},{\"title\":\"Google OR-Tools: operations_research::sat::CpModelPresolver Class Reference\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/cpp/classoperations__research_1_1sat_1_1CpModelPresolver.html\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Presolve time limit · google/or-tools · Discussion #4280\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/discussions/4280\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding the Log - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/understanding_the_log.html\"},{\"title\":\"CPMpy ortools interface (cpmpy.solvers.ortools) — CPMpy 0.9.24 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/ignace_allocation/api/solvers/ortools.html\"},{\"title\":\"cpmpy/cpmpy/solvers/ortools.py at master · CPMpy/cpmpy\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/CPMpy/cpmpy/blob/master/cpmpy/solvers/ortools.py\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's information about the CP-SAT presolve parameters you're asking about:\n\n## CP-SAT Presolve Parameters\n\n### cp_model_probing_level\nThis parameter has a default value of 2. Probing is a technique that tries to fix variables and observe the outcome. Valid values include 0 (to disable probing), 1, 2, and possibly 3 or higher.\n\n### symmetry_level\nThe symmetry_level parameter has a default value of 2. A value of 1 means only do symmetry breaking in presolve, with 0 also being a possible option. Symmetry detection is run before more complex presolve rules as many of them are heuristic based and might break the symmetry present in the original problems.\n\n### Placement (Variable Selection Strategy)\nCP-SAT can be configured to determine how to branch (or make a decision) whenever it can no longer deduce anything via propagation, by providing a list of the variables, defining which variable should be selected next, and defining which value should be probed. Variable selection options include: CHOOSE_FIRST, CHOOSE_LOWEST_MIN, CHOOSE_HIGHEST_MAX, CHOOSE_MIN_DOMAIN_SIZE, and CHOOSE_MAX_DOMAIN_SIZE.\n\n## Related Presolve Parameters\nAdditional presolve control parameters include presolve_probing_deterministic_time_limit (default: 30.0), max_presolve_iterations (default: 3), and probing_deterministic_time_limit (default: 1.0).\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"fce32e81-af53-451d-996b-7edae1d64c82","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:41:19.631Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c44e796b-d5cd-4625-bfcf-1965dee1b368","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"9704b4b0-99b6-4e2e-913c-257ed7c23815","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"fa4d4bc6-e2b2-445f-8cd0-cc97f0106215","agentId":"a37cf00dce550f097","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MwYQomZ6WJm39cDqj4zgaf","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"energetic reasoning\" rectangle packing infeasibility detection cumulative\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"A faster checker of the energetic reasoning for the cumulative scheduling problem | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/351609359_A_faster_checker_of_the_energetic_reasoning_for_the_cumulative_scheduling_problem\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) An Approximative Criterion for the Potential of Energetic Reasoning\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/221452900_An_Approximative_Criterion_for_the_Potential_of_Energetic_Reasoning\"},{\"title\":\"An Approximative Criterion for the Potential of Energetic Reasoning - ADS\",\"url\":\"https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/2011LNCS.6595..229B/abstract\"},{\"title\":\"A new constraint programming approach for the orthogonal packing problem - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0305054806001419\"},{\"title\":\"[1310.5564] The Energetic Reasoning Checker Revisited\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/1310.5564\"},{\"title\":\"A more powerful energetic reasoning for the Cumulative ...\",\"url\":\"https://hal.science/hal-03595219/document\"},{\"title\":\"Energetic reasoning and bin-packing problem, for bounding a parallel machine scheduling problem | 4OR | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10288-006-0017-1\"},{\"title\":\"Energetic reasoning and bin-packing problem, for bounding a parallel machine scheduling problem | Semantic Scholar\",\"url\":\"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/Energetic-reasoning-and-bin-packing-problem,-for-a-Tercinet-N%C3%A9ron/10bfee7cf2858a900dd1c305e631bd229586dd04\"},{\"title\":\"More powerful energetic reasoning for the cumulative scheduling problem - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0166218X25004068\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) A more powerful energetic reasoning for the Cumulative Scheduling Problem\",\"url\":\"https://www.academia.edu/114125434/A_more_powerful_energetic_reasoning_for_the_Cumulative_Scheduling_Problem?uc-sb-sw=26797487\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about energetic reasoning for rectangle packing and infeasibility detection:\n\n## Overview\n\nEnergetic reasoning is an efficient filtering technique for the Cumulative Scheduling Problem. The research in this area extends these concepts to related problems including rectangle packing.\n\n## Application to Rectangle Packing\n\nEnergetic reasoning has been generalized to allow the feasibility of orthogonal packing patterns to be tested. Examples of applications include the cumulative scheduling problem, perfect square problems, strip packing problems, and incomparable rectangles packing problems.\n\n## Infeasibility Detection\n\nIf the energy E(a,b) exceeds (b−a)·C, then the problem is infeasible. This is a fundamental principle used in energetic reasoning for detecting infeasibility in cumulative resource constraints.\n\n## Computational Challenges\n\nEnergetic reasoning is one of the most powerful propagation algorithms in cumulative scheduling; however, it is not commonly used in practice because it has a high running time and its success highly depends on the tightness of the variable bounds.\n\n## Recent Improvements\n\nRecent research has focused on improving the efficiency of energetic reasoning checkers. An O(n×α(n)×log⁡n) checker for energetic reasoning has been introduced, improving upon the previous best technique of O(nlog²⁡n) achieved by Ouellet and Quimper.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"2bfaec74-c0bb-4a45-925e-5621b0171d6b","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:41:20.139Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9704b4b0-99b6-4e2e-913c-257ed7c23815","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"1ad534c7-df49-45f4-a8ba-889e1872eb51","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"fa4d4bc6-e2b2-445f-8cd0-cc97f0106215","agentId":"a37cf00dce550f097","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014kWC5hS48TsXqmajW4ZXkv","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"facility location grid placement multi-commodity flow precheck infeasibility\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"The Online Multi-Commodity Facility Location Problem∗ Jannik Castenow\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2005.08391\"},{\"title\":\"Integrated facility location and capacity planning under uncertainty | Computational and Applied Mathematics | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s40314-021-01560-0\"},{\"title\":\"Facility location problem - Cornell University Computational Optimization Open Textbook - Optimization Wiki\",\"url\":\"https://optimization.cbe.cornell.edu/index.php?title=Facility_location_problem\"},{\"title\":\"Approximation Algorithms for Single and Multi-Commodity Connected Facility Location | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-642-20807-2_20\"},{\"title\":\"Facility location problems — Mathematical Optimization: Solving Problems using Gurobi and Python\",\"url\":\"https://scipbook.readthedocs.io/en/latest/flp.html\"},{\"title\":\"Two-Stage Robust Network Flow and Design under Demand Uncertainty – Optimization Online\",\"url\":\"https://optimization-online.org/2005/02/1069/\"},{\"title\":\"The capacitated plant location problem with multiple facilities in the same site | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/222148601_The_capacitated_plant_location_problem_with_multiple_facilities_in_the_same_site\"},{\"title\":\"The Online Multi-Commodity Facility Location Problem - ADS\",\"url\":\"https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/2020arXiv200508391C/abstract\"},{\"title\":\"Facility location problem - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Facility_location_problem\"},{\"title\":\"Multi-commodity location-routing: Flow intercepting formulation and branch-and-cut algorithm - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0305054817302204\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found related to your query on facility location, grid placement, multi-commodity flow, and precheck infeasibility:\n\n## Key Findings:\n\n**Multi-Commodity Facility Location**: The Multi-Commodity Facility Location Problem (MFLP) is a natural extension to the metric uncapacitated Facility Location Problem in which requests ask for different commodities, and was introduced by Ravi and Sinha in 2004.\n\n**Problem Structure**: In this model, requests are located at points of a finite metric space and algorithms must construct facilities and assign requests to facilities while minimizing construction cost and assignment distances. Requests and facilities are heterogeneous, requesting or offering multiple commodities, and a request must be connected to a set of facilities jointly offering the commodities demanded by it. Algorithms must decide not only if and where to place facilities, but also which commodities to offer at each.\n\n**Integration with Multi-Commodity Flow**: Multi-commodity facility location problems can be reformulated according to a multi-commodity flow formalism and decomposed through Lagrangean relaxation into a master facility location problem and a slave minimal cost multi-commodity flow problem.\n\n**Robustness and Feasibility**: Two-stage robust optimization approaches for network flow and design problems give upper bounds on the probability of infeasibility, can be generalized to multi-commodity flow and design, and apply to facility location problems.\n\nThe search results don't contain specific information about \"grid placement\" or \"precheck infeasibility\" as distinct technical concepts in this context. If you're looking for more specific technical papers on these exact terms, you may need to search with more specialized or recent academic terminology.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"dce3eb59-c6eb-4e2c-a2c9-05b6f0d27581","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:41:21.012Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"1ad534c7-df49-45f4-a8ba-889e1872eb51","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
