{"parentUuid":"ba9dde2f-c37b-4262-a095-36a1a040b44f","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a37cf00dce550f097","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_019URi1S7FGPtpvcvJsqWfFL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DG84uSkhpXpsEWs2NXzuYy","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto","prompt":"List all parameters related to: presolve, probing, symmetry, no_overlap_2d, packing, and dual_feasible. For each, give the parameter name, default value, and what it does. Focus on parameters that might help speed up 2D rectangle packing problems."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2614,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1681,"cache_read_input_tokens":33023,"output_tokens":416,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1681},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2614,"output_tokens":416,"cache_read_input_tokens":33023,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1681,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1681,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaorfeNkrc9cFX14hHAwT","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"a1967da4-57e4-4e5a-9212-d83a7c120027","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:41:48.181Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"d0c30b18-d09e-43e1-8b2c-8df7afd6aabd","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"fa4d4bc6-e2b2-445f-8cd0-cc97f0106215","agentId":"a37cf00dce550f097","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BxozeFY5erJX9yEHvcgCzE","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"two-dimensional bin packing\" reduction procedure necessary condition area corner\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Algorithms for the two dimensional bin packing problem ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.numdam.org/article/RO_2012__46_1_41_0.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"New reduction procedures and lower bounds for the two-dimensional bin packing problem with fixed orientation | Computers and Operations Research\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/abs/10.1016/j.cor.2005.08.012\"},{\"title\":\"Bin packing problem - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bin_packing_problem\"},{\"title\":\"New reduction procedures and lower bounds for the two-dimensional bin packing problem with fixed orientation - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0305054805002765\"},{\"title\":\"Positions and covering: A two-stage methodology to obtain optimal solutions for the 2d-bin packing problem | PLOS One\",\"url\":\"https://journals.plos.org/plosone/article?id=10.1371%2Fjournal.pone.0229358\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) New reduction procedures and lower bounds for the two-dimensional bin packing problem with fixed orientation\",\"url\":\"https://www.academia.edu/15186649/New_reduction_procedures_and_lower_bounds_for_the_two_dimensional_bin_packing_problem_with_fixed_orientation\"},{\"title\":\"The two-dimensional bin packing problem with variable bin sizes and costs - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1572528605000216\"},{\"title\":\"An introduction to the two‐dimensional rectangular cutting and packing problem - Oliveira - 2023 - International Transactions in Operational Research - Wiley Online Library\",\"url\":\"https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1111/itor.13236\"},{\"title\":\"A new exact method for the two-dimensional bin-packing problem with\",\"url\":\"https://www.math.u-bordeaux.fr/~fclautia/publications/clautiaux_et_al_ORL_exact.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Robust Optimization for the Two-Dimensional Strip-Packing Problem with Variable-Sized Bins\",\"url\":\"https://www.mdpi.com/2227-7390/11/23/4781\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about two-dimensional bin packing and reduction procedures. Here's what the research shows:\n\n## Two-Dimensional Bin Packing and Reduction Procedures\n\nThe two-dimensional bin-packing problem (2BP) consists of minimizing the number of identical rectangles used to pack a set of smaller rectangles.\n\n### Reduction Procedures\n\nNew reduction procedures are described which are used to reduce the size of the instance and can be applied as a preprocessing step before applying a heuristic or an exact method. Identically-feasible functions (IFF) can be used to modify the size of the items without changing the value of OPT, showing that the initial instance can be reduced by removing small items and by increasing the size of the large items.\n\n### Area and Corner Considerations\n\nLower bounds for 2BP are based on the total area of the items after application of dual feasible functions (DFF).\n\nRegarding corner positioning, a Cartesian coordinate system is used where the origin (0, 0) is located at the bin bottom left corner, with the x-axis for horizontal locations and the y-axis for vertical positions coinciding with the bin edges, and the position of an item is expressed as the coordinates of its bottom-left corner in the bin.\n\nThe research indicates that reduction procedures are essential preprocessing steps for solving the two-dimensional bin packing problem, with area-based metrics and corner positioning being fundamental concepts in the problem formulation.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"baff2944-28d9-40d3-a2a3-d0574b0b8588","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:41:50.710Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d0c30b18-d09e-43e1-8b2c-8df7afd6aabd","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"17ef8a28-4ee4-42a6-9327-60450f07908e","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"fa4d4bc6-e2b2-445f-8cd0-cc97f0106215","agentId":"a37cf00dce550f097","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QDWv7hhj72Pv99SHtVZx6x","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"strip packing\" preprocessing valid inequalities plate cutting necessary conditions\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Mixed-integer programming models for irregular strip packing based on vertical slices and feasibility cuts - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0377221723006148\"},{\"title\":\"Exact solutions for the 2d-strip packing problem using the positions-and-covering methodology - PMC\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7808675/\"},{\"title\":\"An exact approach for the two-dimensional strip packing problem with defects - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0360835225000117\"},{\"title\":\"Mixed-integer programming models for irregular strip packing based on vertical slices and feasibility cuts\",\"url\":\"https://ideas.repec.org/a/eee/ejores/v313y2024i1p69-91.html\"},{\"title\":\"A new mixed-integer programming model for irregular strip ...\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2206.00032\"},{\"title\":\"Enhanced solution for the irregular strip packing problem: valid inequalities and branching priorities | Galoá Proceedings\",\"url\":\"https://proceedings.science/sbpo/sbpo-2021/papers/enhanced-solution-for-the-irregular-strip-packing-problem-valid-inequalities-and?lang=en\"},{\"title\":\"Exact solutions for the 2d-strip packing problem using the positions-and-covering methodology | PLOS One\",\"url\":\"https://journals.plos.org/plosone/article?id=10.1371/journal.pone.0245267\"},{\"title\":\"Robust mixed-integer linear programming models for the irregular strip packing problem | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/297889945_Robust_mixed-integer_linear_programming_models_for_the_irregular_strip_packing_problem\"},{\"title\":\"Exact solution techniques for two-dimensional cutting and packing - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0377221720306111\"},{\"title\":\"Enhanced solution for the irregular strip packing problem: valid inequalities\",\"url\":\"https://repositorio.usp.br/bitstreams/83b7bc41-fac2-413f-b6f7-deab749a57b7\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about strip packing, preprocessing techniques, valid inequalities, and cutting/packing problems. Here's what the research shows:\n\n## Strip Packing and Related Techniques\n\nThe irregular strip-packing problem, also known as nesting or marker making, is defined as the automatic computation of a non-overlapping placement of a set of non-convex polygons onto a rectangular strip of fixed width and unbounded length, such that the strip length is minimized.\n\n## Valid Inequalities\n\nValid inequalities are derived from a convex decomposition of the feasible space of relative placements between pieces, along with symmetry breakings and variable eliminations. Set-covering formulations for the strip packing problem can be strengthened with families of valid inequalities.\n\n## Preprocessing Techniques\n\nPreprocessing methods for cutting and packing problems are considerably fast compared to the overall solution time and may reduce the size of instances, thus simplifying their resolution. Customized preprocessing techniques, lower bounding methods, and valid inequalities are employed to enhance solution approaches.\n\n## Cutting and Packing Problems\n\nThe research indicates that cutting and packing are closely related problem classes. In the two-dimensional strip packing problem, items are typically placed without the guillotine cut constraint. The necessity of guillotine cuts (which restrict cuts to be made orthogonally across the entire material) depends on specific problem variants and application requirements.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"fa082574-1fd0-4649-969a-fd67a1fed781","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:41:51.833Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"17ef8a28-4ee4-42a6-9327-60450f07908e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"ba9dde2f-c37b-4262-a095-36a1a040b44f","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"fa4d4bc6-e2b2-445f-8cd0-cc97f0106215","agentId":"a37cf00dce550f097","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FrSVdtEtk8xmoXmBnv25b1","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"corner points\" placement positions packing dominance Christofides Whitlock\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Extreme Point-Based Heuristics for Three-Dimensional Bin ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.cirrelt.ca/documentstravail/cirrelt-2007-41.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"An Algorithm for Two-Dimensional Cutting Problems | Operations Research\",\"url\":\"https://pubsonline.informs.org/doi/abs/10.1287/opre.25.1.30\"},{\"title\":\"Exact algorithms for the two-dimensional guillotine knapsack - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0305054811000190\"},{\"title\":\"Positions and covering: A two-stage methodology to obtain optimal solutions for the 2d-bin packing problem | PLOS One\",\"url\":\"https://journals.plos.org/plosone/article?id=10.1371%2Fjournal.pone.0229358\"},{\"title\":\"An Algorithm for Two-Dimensional Cutting Problems\",\"url\":\"https://ideas.repec.org/a/inm/oropre/v25y1977i1p30-44.html\"},{\"title\":\"New and improved level heuristics for the rectangular strip packing and variable-sized bin packing problems - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0377221709005360\"},{\"title\":\"Christofides algorithm - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christofides_algorithm\"},{\"title\":\"Guillotine cutting | Detailed Pedia\",\"url\":\"https://detailedpedia.com/wiki-Guillotine_cutting\"},{\"title\":\"Packing Problem - an overview | ScienceDirect Topics\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/computer-science/packing-problem\"},{\"title\":\"A dominance criterion for packing problems - Archive ouverte HAL\",\"url\":\"https://hal.science/hal-01027784\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about this topic. Here's what the research reveals:\n\nNicos Christofides and Charles Whitlock published \"An Algorithm for Two-Dimensional Cutting Problems\" in 1977. Christofides and Whitlock proposed exact approaches for the guillotine two-dimensional knapsack problem (G2KP), which is a guillotine two-dimensional single large object placement problem (2D-SLOPP).\n\nRegarding placement positions and packing, the main idea of the Positions stage in the Positions and Covering (P&C) methodology is to generate the dominant set of valid positions where items can be placed into a bin, which from the infinite set of all possible positions, constructs only a finite set that guarantees the optimality of the solution.\n\nWith respect to corner points specifically, the Extreme Points idea extends the Corner Points concept and provides the means to exploit the free space defined inside a packing by the shapes of the items already in the container.\n\nChristofides and Whitlock presented tree-search procedures for unstaged guillotine cutting, contributing significantly to the field of two-dimensional cutting and packing problems.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"ddcd6182-719f-4f69-9ac1-48a0c44492f4","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:41:52.108Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ba9dde2f-c37b-4262-a095-36a1a040b44f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"a1967da4-57e4-4e5a-9212-d83a7c120027","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"fa4d4bc6-e2b2-445f-8cd0-cc97f0106215","agentId":"a37cf00dce550f097","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DG84uSkhpXpsEWs2NXzuYy","type":"tool_result","content":"# SAT Solver Parameters for 2D Rectangle Packing\n\nBased on the `sat_parameters.proto` file, here are relevant parameters for optimizing 2D rectangle packing problems:\n\n## Presolve Parameters\n\n**cp_model_presolve** (default: true)\nEnables preprocessing of the CP model before solving, which simplifies the problem structure.\n\n**cp_model_probing_level** (default: 2)\nControls effort spent on probing, where 0 disables it completely and higher values increase preprocessing intensity.\n\n**cp_model_use_sat_presolve** (default: true)\nApplies SAT-specific preprocessing techniques when CP model presolving is enabled.\n\n**max_presolve_iterations** (default: 3)\nLimits how many presolve iterations occur when significant reductions are detected.\n\n## Probing Parameters\n\n**probing_deterministic_time_limit** (default: 1.0)\nSets maximum deterministic time for probing in CP-SAT solving.\n\n**presolve_probing_deterministic_time_limit** (default: 30.0)\nSpecifies time budget for probing during the presolve phase.\n\n## No-Overlap Constraint Parameters\n\n**use_strong_propagation_in_disjunctive** (default: false)\nEnables stronger but more expensive propagation on no-overlap constraints, useful for packing.\n\n**use_dynamic_precedence_in_disjunctive** (default: false)\nAllows branching on interval precedence decisions rather than just bounds.\n\n**max_size_to_create_precedence_literals_in_disjunctive** (default: 60)\nCreates literals for task pair disjunctions when interval count is below this threshold.\n\n**use_precedences_in_disjunctive_constraint** (default: true)\nLeverages precedence relations between intervals for enhanced propagation in scheduling.\n\n## Performance Tuning\n\nFor 2D rectangle packing, enabling stronger propagation options and adjusting probing levels typically helps, though with trade-offs between solution quality and runtime."}]},"uuid":"e361458f-52df-4c50-8800-69866794bd8f","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:41:54.193Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a1967da4-57e4-4e5a-9212-d83a7c120027","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
